Yes, you are right with "*thousands* of turns" but you are wrong WRT "the
early game"; in the early game - the focus of the thread - errors are
typically often either instant deadly, or set the stage for more problems
that easily lead to death.

As I said above; "That clearly depends on the type of error and how far
you are in the game."

You want an example? From one of my games; shooting at a horde of elves
in minetown, inadvertently hitting a soldier, etc. - you certainly know
how such a mistake can evolve once you are surrounded by non-Elbereth
respecting guards, if you have not yet effective options to choose from
to escape or fix the problem.

Yes, you are right that this is typically not deadly "thousands of turns
later" (or in a later stage of a game), but often you'll die just a few
dozens of turns later if such mistakes happen in the early game.

Yes, folks; play careful.

